      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="697250887">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-06-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP730 - Sails, Rails and Tails

Posted: N54° 27.258' W110° 09.904'

MyGPSr: N54° 27.260' W110° 09.906'

(FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The park this cap lives in was just bustling with activity when I arrived. There were kids everywhere, doing what kids do best: run, jump, scream, dash, fall and do it all over again in a different order. Good on them!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I'd seen context shots of this one before arriving and was expecting a dead easy find, but you know that huge X in the grass has faded a lot and I had to work a bit to find the cap. Poor me, eh?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="621798568">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="54.454300" lon="-110.165067" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="321730">Sleepy_hollow</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP730 Sails, Rails &amp; Tails&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After a little over night rain we emerged from the tent ready to check out a few caps in the Cold Lake vicinity. The newer of the two caps we hadn't found was set up for the recent mega. We found the arena, ball diamond and in fairly short order the near by cap - thanks OFTH for setting it up!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="621224431">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3355355">CachingCarolandHugh</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP730 – Sails, Rails &amp; Tails&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posted: N54º 27.258  W110º 09.904&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Elevation: 659.4 M&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPSr:    N 54º 27.260  W110º 09.904&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Elevation: 553&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks &lt;strong&gt;outforthehunt&lt;/strong&gt; for adding this Brass Cap for the Sails, Rails and Tails 2016 (WESTCAN6) Mega event in Cold Lake. As we mentioned in our email, don't know why the elevations between the posted and our GPSr differ by such amount.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We had gone up to Cold Lake on Tuesday July 5th to attend the Sails, Rails &amp; Tails 2016 (WESTCAN6) Mega event. Then stayed over at the RV park we were at, for another week to do some more caching and take in the Cold Lake Air Show the following weekend. We logged a lot of caches found and with the satellite event in places like Elk Point and Glendon were also able to find some of the Brass Caps in Cold Lake and area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thanks for the Brass Cap &quot;outforthehunt &quot; &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_tongue.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;...CachingCarolandHugh &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_approve.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
